    "“%@” didn't move your %@ this week. A week is weak evidence — you can try again." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“%@” no movió tu %@ en esta semana. Una semana es poca evidencia, puedes volver a intentarlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” raised your %@ this week. We marked it as proven in What works for you." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“%@” subió tu %@ en la semana. La marcamos como probada en Lo que funciona en ti."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "«%@» tends to coincide with higher stress." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«%@» tends to coincide with higher stress."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«%@» tiende a coincidir con tu estrés alto."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "«%@» tends to coincide with lower stress." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«%@» tends to coincide with lower stress."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«%@» tiende a coincidir con tu estrés bajo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "«Calm time» is the share of the last month that sat in the Low band; «steadiness» is how much your daily index varies week to week (its coefficient of variation — lower is steadier). The Low / Moderate / High bands (0–1 / 1–2 / 2–3) are the same for everyone because the index is already adjusted to your own baseline. (Plews 2013)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«Calm time» is the share of the last month that sat in the Low band; «steadiness» is how much your daily index varies week to week (its coefficient of variation — lower is steadier). The Low / Moderate / High bands (0–1 / 1–2 / 2–3) are the same for everyone because the index is already adjusted to your own baseline. (Plews 2013)"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«Tiempo en calma» es la parte del último mes que pasó en la banda Baja; «estabilidad» es cuánto varía tu índice diario de una semana a otra (su coeficiente de variación, más bajo, más estable). Las bandas Baja / Moderada / Alta (0–1 / 1–2 / 2–3) son iguales para todos porque el índice ya está ajustado a tu propia base. (Plews 2013)"
          }
        }
      }
